-- ============================================================================
-- 1. Crystal Polymorphism & Kinetic Trapping (Open Problem #4)
-- ============================================================================
-- A crystal energy landscape has conformations C, an energy E : C → Nat, and a
-- barrier-bounded transition relation step : C → C → Bool that only permits moves
-- staying below kinetic thermal budget B : Nat (barrier(c, c') ≤ B).
-- A basin predicate InBasin : C → Type 0 is kinetically trapped at budget B if no
-- allowed transition can exit InBasin (every barrier out exceeds B).
KineticTrap : (C : Type 0) → (C → C → Bool) → (C → Type 0) → Type 0
KineticTrap C step InBasin =
  (a b : C) → InBasin a → step a b ≡ true → InBasin b
